<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	The widget extension: a standard sandboxed extension, as iGhostVT's is.
	It draws what it is given and opens nothing else: the Live Activity's
	state comes from ActivityKit, and the home screen widget reads the one
	snapshot the app writes into the App Group container both carry
	(`group.wiki.qaq.apelin`, Widgets/Shared/ChatWidgetSnapshot.swift), the
	way Fila's save action shares Fila's. The sandbox keeps it out of
	mobile's Documents, where the app keeps everything else, and the app has
	no container of its own to share.

	Nothing that widens it: no `no-sandbox`, `platform-application`,
	container or storage keys, no mach lookup and above all no
	`wiki.qaq.apelin.client` — apelind must never accept a connection from
	anything but the app. Scripts/package-deb.sh reads the signed
	entitlements back and fails on any of them.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>application-identifier</key>
	<string>wiki.qaq.apelin.widgets</string>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.wiki.qaq.apelin</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
